-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the moduli place of a Γ₀(N)-class
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field with decidable equality, and let $N$ be a positive natural number with $(N:K)\neq 0$. Let $x$ be a moduli point of level $N$ over $K$, i.e. a class in the quotient of the type of data consisting of a Weierstrass curve over $K$ that is elliptic together with an affine point of exact additive order $N$, modulo the relation generated by applying a variable change and replacing the point by $k$ times its transport for some $k$ coprime to $N$. Let $v$ and $v'$ be places of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,K\,N$ over $K$ — that is, valuation subrings, proper, containing the image of $K$, and principal ideal rings — of the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ obtained by adjoining to $K$ the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,K\,d\,(\mathrm{jqModC}\,K)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$. Assume each of $v$, $v'$ satisfies `IsModuliPlaceOf K N x`: there is an extension field $\Omega$ of $K$ and a moduli test datum for $x$ over $\Omega$ (a place $W$ of $\Omega$, a Weierstrass curve over the valuation ring of $W$ with nonvanishing discriminant after reduction, a point of exact order $N$ on it over $\Omega$ reducing to a representative of $x$ via a residue-field retraction, and a $K$-embedding $\mathrm{emb}$ of the modular function field into $\Omega$ pinned by the cyclic-quotient $j$-values of the generator) whose valuation subring pulls back along $\mathrm{emb}$ to that of the place. Then $v = v'$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the correspondence between $\Gamma_0(N)$-structures over $K$ and places of the modular function field: the place attached to a class $(E_0,C)$ by a test datum depends only on the class, not on the chosen model, generator or ambient valued extension. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd and Diamond-style place-by-place comparisons of modular curves, where places of the level-$N$ function field must be indexed by moduli data.
